ImportError|ERROR" /tmp/web_chat_1.txt | head -20 Expected: FAIL with ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'web_chat' . [ ] Step 3: Create web_chat.py with the routes and the stream Create apps/predbat/web_chat.py with the house header and: """The Chat tab: its page, its routes and its server-sent event stream. Which conversation a browser is looking at is client state, passed on every request, so two browsers never fight over a shared cursor. The only global server state is the single active turn, and busy/idle events reach every browser whatever conversation it is viewing - which is what lets a user read another conversation while a turn runs. """ import asyncio import json from aiohttp import web from chat import AgentNotReadyError, ChatBusyError SSE_POLL_SECONDS = 0.1 SSE_HEARTBEAT_SECONDS = 15 def format_sse_event(event): """Render one buffered event as an SSE frame.""" return "id: {}
event: {}
